libusb 1.0.30 (https://libusb.info), in the Windows and Mac packages only (libusb/, unmodified binaries: the official
Windows build from https://github.com/libusb/libusb/releases, Homebrew's macOS bottles), for NovaStar's own USB device.
Copyright the libusb authors (AUTHORS in its source), GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1 or later —
licenses/libusb-COPYING.txt. Its source: https://github.com/libusb/libusb/releases/download/v1.0.30/libusb-1.0.30.tar.bz2
(SHA-256 fea36f34f9156400209595e300840767ab1a385ede1dc7ee893015aea9c6dbaf). Open Nova loads it at run time
(tools/novalink.py); replacing it with another build of libusb works the same.

USBPcap 1.5.4.0 (https://desowin.org/usbpcap/), in the Windows package only (usb-capture/): the official installer
USBPcapSetup-1.5.4.0.exe, unmodified (SHA-256 87a7edf9bbbcf07b5f4373d9a192a6770d2ff3add7aa1e276e82e38582ccb622), and the
complete source of that release, usbpcap-src-incl-pdb-1.5.4.0.7z (also at https://github.com/desowin/usbpcap/tree/1.5.4.0).
Copyright (c) 2013-2020 Tomasz Moń. The driver (USBPcap.sys) is under the GNU General Public License 2.0 —
licenses/USBPcap-GPL-2.0.txt; USBPcapCMD.exe under the BSD 2-Clause licence — licenses/USBPcap-BSD-2-Clause.txt. It is a
separate program: Open Nova only starts its installer when you click "Install USB capture…", and USBPcapCMD.exe to record
USB (tools/usbcap.py).

Open Nova runs on the Python standard library and the browser; libusb above is its only other runtime library, and only
for USB (USBPcap is a separate program, optional, Windows only).

